## Appendix A: Example Configurations

### Minimal Configuration
```yaml
todofile: README.md
projects:
  - name: default
    title: TODO
    parent: nil
```

### Multi-Project Configuration
```yaml
todofile: README.md
projects:
  - name: default
    title: TODO
    parent: nil
  - name: bugs
    title: Bug Tracker
    parent: nil
  - name: features
    title: Feature Requests
    parent: nil
  - name: frontend
    title: Frontend
    parent: features
  - name: backend
    title: Backend
    parent: features
```

### Deep Nesting Configuration
```yaml
todofile: docs/TASKS.md
projects:
  - name: lego
    title: Lego Projects
    parent: nil
  - name: technic
    title: Technic Sets
    parent: lego
  - name: vehicles
    title: Vehicles
    parent: technic
  - name: construction
    title: Construction Vehicles
    parent: vehicles
```

## Appendix B: Markdown Examples

### Simple TODO
```markdown
# TODO

- [ ] Task 1
- [X] Task 2
- [ ] FIXME: Critical issue
```

### Nested Projects
```markdown
# Lego Projects

Some intro text about the Lego projects.

## Technic Sets

- [ ] Buy crane set
- [ ] Build crane model
- [X] Organize parts

## City Sets

- [ ] Build police station
- [ ] FIXME: Missing pieces in fire truck set
```

### Mixed Content
```markdown
# My Project

This is a regular markdown document with various content.

## Overview

Some documentation here.

## TODO

- [ ] Write tests
- [ ] Update README
- [X] Fix bug #123

## Architecture

More documentation.

### Database Schema

- Tables
- Relationships

## Bugs

- [ ] FIXME: Memory leak in parser
- [ ] Performance issue with large files

## Conclusion

Final thoughts.
```

## Appendix C: Glossary

- **Project**: A named container for TODO items with a title and optional parent
- **Topic**: Synonym for TODO item
- **FIXME**: High-priority TODO item prefixed with "FIXME:" or "fixme:"
- **Parent**: The project that contains another project in the hierarchy
- **Level**: The markdown header level (1-6) corresponding to nesting depth
- **Configuration**: The `.mktodo.yml` file defining projects and settings
- **Git Root**: The top-level directory of the git repository containing `.git/`

